## What this skill provides

Bulleted list of specific capabilities — routing decisions, checks, Wolfram
entry points, references.

## Layer routing

How this topic lands on atperson's layers:

- **C23 core (`include/atperson/`, `src/core/`)** — what, if anything, this
  topic means for the learning graph. Usually nothing: atperson core consumes
  distilled observations only.
- **C++23 runtime (`src/app/`)** — which Wolfram entry points are called here
  (e.g. `AtprotoClient` calling `wf_agent_get_timeline`), how return values
  and RAII are handled, what JSON/cJSON extraction produces.
- **Wolfram (pinned revision)** — the mechanics live here; never re-implement
  them. Point at `wolfram/README.md`.

## Defaults

The invariants that hold regardless of layer. Keep to 3–6 bullets. Example:

- **<Wire rule>** — one-line normative rule. Link to `shared/<file>.md`.
- **<Wolfram entry point>** — one-line rule naming the header/function.
- **<Key edge case>** — the thing that bites everyone once.

## Reading guide

For every <topic> task:

1. Read the relevant `shared/*.md` first. They define the protocol rules.
2. Read `wolfram/README.md` for the API mapping at the pinned revision.
3. Read the matching `src/app/` integration (e.g. `atproto_client.cpp`) when
   the task touches the runtime.

Always prefer the Wolfram call over hand-rolling: this is AGENTS.md policy.

## Hazards to flag up front

High-frequency failure modes specific to atperson + Wolfram. Short entries,
one line of context each. Examples:

- **Never let the C core see AT Protocol types.** Observations must be
  distilled primitives (text, URI, DID, timestamp) before crossing into C23.
- **`wf_*` returns `wf_status`; check `WF_OK` and free owned outputs** with
  the documented free function. RAII wrappers live in `src/app/`.
- **<Wire field> omitted vs null divergence.** Signatures produced by one impl
  may not verify through another.
- **Read-only network:** skills must not describe write flows for the learning
  graph (no posts/replies/moderations as learning side effects).

## Verification

Clone-agnostic checks for this topic:

- Offline parsers/validators in Wolfram that work without a network
  (`wf_cid_from_string`, `wf_syntax_*_is_valid`, `wf_did_document_parse`,
  `wf_validate_record`, `wf_car_parse`, …).
- Core-only build/tests:
  ```sh
  cmake -S . -B build-core -DATPERSON_BUILD_NETWORK=OFF
  cmake --build build-core -j
  ctest --test-dir build-core --output-on-failure
  ```
- Network-enabled build/tests when the topic touches `src/app/`:
  `cmake -S . -B build-net -DATPERSON_BUILD_NETWORK=ON` then build + ctest.

